    familyAdventure: "Cook together using ratios. Find a recipe and discuss the ratios: if it says 2 cups flour and 1 cup sugar, the ratio is 2:1. Then scale the recipe: make a half batch (ratio stays the same, amounts halve) or double batch. Taste both — do they taste the same? Then calculate unit prices at the grocery: a 12-oz box costs $3.60 and a 16-oz box costs $4.00. Which is the better deal? (Calculate price per ounce: $0.30 vs $0.25 — the bigger box is cheaper per ounce.) Ratios are the math of smart shopping.",
